# M5 WARP-only + Apple + Microsoft Defender services (carmel)

## Preferred posture

1. **Quit ProtonVPN** (app may linger — default route must **not** be Proton WireGuard `utun`).
2. **Cloudflare WARP** enrolled **Organization: centexmsp**, status **Connected**, mode **`WarpWithDnsOverHttps`** (`warp-cli mode warp+doh`).
3. Confirm: `curl -sS https://www.cloudflare.com/cdn-cgi/trace` → **`warp=on` `gateway=on`**.
4. GitHub plain path: `./scripts/diagnose-m5-github-dns.sh` → plain curl **200** when WARP DNS stubs healthy.

## Do not invent parallel VPN stacks

- Preferred ZT path = **WARP + Gateway** (Access-controlled Team).
- Proton is **legacy coexistence** only; dual-stack caused dead DNS (`127.0.2.2`) historically — see [OPERATOR_SESSION_START_AND_IDE_REALITY_SSOT.md](https://github.com/centexmsp/repository-restructuring/blob/main/docs/OPERATOR_SESSION_START_AND_IDE_REALITY_SSOT.md) **§D**.

## Apple / iMessage / Hide My Email

| Symptom | Likely cause | Action |
|---------|--------------|--------|
| Apple ID / iCloud login **stuck** | Usually **not** MITM (re-probe first) | `./scripts/diagnose-m5-warp-apple-services.sh`; issuer must be **Apple**. Prefer **named SNI DNI** list **Centex Apple iCloud AppleID - Do Not Inspect hosts** (keep CDN **in tunnel**). Quit **ProtonVPN** fully. Bounce: `killall appleaccountd accountsd akd cloudd`. See OPERATOR **§D.6.1** |
| Apple ID cannot sign in | Auth hosts MITM or IdP | Same diag; if issuer is **Gateway CA** → extend DNI list (named FQDN only) |
| iMessage offline | APNs UDP/TCP via tunnel | Split exclude **`17.0.0.0/8`** on device profiles (already program default) |
| Hide My Email broken | **`mask.icloud.com` → Akamai `172.224/12` outside 17/8** | **Narrow** host split-tunnel: `mask.icloud.com`, `mask-h2.icloud.com`, `mask-api.icloud.com`, `*.apple-dns.net` + DNI list (not Akamai CIDR) |
| curl mask TLS `illegal parameter` with route on **en0** | Apple/Akamai client TLS (not CF MITM) | Test in **System Settings**; CLI LibreSSL is not authoritative |

## Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (macOS) / MAU OneCDN

| Symptom | Likely cause | Action |
|---------|--------------|--------|
| Defender cannot download updates / `wdav-upgrade.pkg` fails | Gateway **TLS decrypt** on Microsoft product CDN (HSTS/pinning-sensitive) | `./scripts/diagnose-m5-warp-microsoft-defender.sh` — OneCDN issuer must be **Microsoft**, not **Gateway CA** |
| `https://res.public.onecdn.static.microsoft/.../MacAutoupdate/wdav-upgrade.pkg` blocked or untrusted | Same MITM class as Apple CDN | Named DOMAIN list **Centex Microsoft macOS Defender MAU - Do Not Inspect hosts** + HTTP rule **Centex Microsoft macOS Defender/MAU - Do Not Inspect** (`action=off`). See OPERATOR **§D.7** |
| Office 365 app DNI alone insufficient | Auto-generated O365 apps ≠ OneCDN product plane | Keep **OS-scoped Microsoft macOS list** separate from generic O365 rule |

### Security balance (mandatory)

1. **Prefer Do Not Inspect** (named FQDNs via **Gateway lists**, one list per OS/vendor plane) over split-tunnel.
2. **Never** add broad Akamai CIDRs (`172.224/12`, bare `akamaiedge.net`, bare `edgekey.net`) — multi-tenant unknown hosting.
3. **Do not** DNI bare parent **`apple.com`** or bare **`microsoft.com`** (too wide); use specific hosts + intentional parents only when justified (`icloud.com`, `cdn-apple.com`, `onecdn.static.microsoft`, `static.microsoft` for product CDN plane).
4. Split-tunnel only for proven gaps (HME Akamai edge + `17/8`). Product CDN stays **in tunnel under DNI**.
5. Name rules **`Centex <Vendor> <OS/plane> - Do Not Inspect`** so multi-tenant Gateway stays auditable.

